# Restoration Seminar: "Return target nonland permanent card from your graveyard to the battlefield." Paradigm: it is exiled as
# it resolves, and at the beginning of each of its owner's first main phases they may cast a copy of it from exile without paying
# its mana cost (CR 702.192a, 707.12). Bot2 Bolts Bot1's Ornithopter on turn 2. Turn 3: Bot1 Strip Mines Bot2's Island - the
# Strip Mine is a land card in the graveyard, which the Seminar cannot target (the refused cast) beside the
# Ornithopter, which it can - and casts the Seminar with four Moxen and a Black Lotus ({5}{W}{W}): the Ornithopter comes back.
# Bot2 Bolts it again on turn 4; on turn 5 the copy is accepted and returns it a second time, the card still in exile.

